{"id":"u-d98eb8c3-c18c-4ffa-90d2-fc42cc8221cc","src":"community","title":"Jiren’s Absolute Power: Upper/Lower","author":"Tuomas S.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/HY6jMp-jirens-absolute-power-upperlower-1","desc":"\"Strength is absolute. Absolute strength overcomes all obstacles, shatters every limit, and bends the multiverse to its will.\" — Jiren the Gray\n\nThis is the exact 4-day Upper/Lower protocol that forged Jiren’s legendary, world-conquering physique.\n\nTo achieve absolute dominance, half-measures are forbidden. Look at Jiren—his power does not come merely from a wide back or a dense chest. His strength is rooted in massive, pillar-like quads, a heavy posterior chain, and lethal arms. You need the full package to conquer the world and defeat Son Goku in the Tournament of Power. If a single muscle group slacks, your power falters.\n\n🔱 The Rules of Absolute Execution\n\nThe Rolling Schedule: This is a continuous 4-day split (Upper A / Lower A / Upper B / Lower B). Perform this 3 or 4 days per week. When the week ends, simply pick up with the next workout day the following week without resetting the cycle.\n\nProgressive Overload: Stagnation is defeat. In every single workout, you must strive to perform more reps or lift more weight than last time. Every extra rep is proof of growing absolute power.\n\nIntensity Over Volume (Jiren Mode): This program is designed with fewer total sets, but every set demands maximum effort. Almost every exercise requires pushing the final set to absolute failure (RPE 10). You earn every single rep.\n\nWarm-up Protocol & Injury Prevention: Perform at least 2–3 warm-up sets before your main work to prepare your joints and tendons. If you experience pain, joint discomfort, or fatigue, dial it back—a true warrior knows when to manage load to fight harder tomorrow.\n\nRest Intervals: Rest 3 minutes between sets on heavy main lifts to ensure total neural recovery. For smaller/isolation movements, rest times can be lower, but never drop under 2 minutes.\n\nAdding Volume (Week 3+): If your recovery is optimal after Week 3 and you demand more challenge, you are allowed to add 1 additional set to isolation/accessory movements (e.g., arms, shoulders, calves, abs). Keep the main heavy lifts at lower set counts to preserve max loading capacity.\n\n📊 Optimized Volume & Structure (No Junk Volume)\nEvery set is executed at max intensity (3 sets for main lifts, 2 sets for accessories). Average session length: 55–70 minutes.\n\nChest: 12 sets\n\nBack / Lats: 12 sets\n\nQuads: 11 sets\n\nHamstrings & Glutes: 11 sets\n\nBiceps: 7 sets\n\nSide & Rear Delts: 6 sets\n\nTriceps: 5 sets\n\nCalves: 5 sets\n\nAbs: 5 sets\n\nAdductors & Abductors: 4 sets\n\n🌌 The Ultimate Evolution\nFollow this protocol with unyielding discipline. After this 10-week program, you will evolve. When you evolve, your power will outclass even Universe 11's God of Destruction.\n\nGood luck!\n\n🔥🔥🔥 What are you waiting for? KNOCK GOKU OUT OF THIS TOURNAMENT NOW! DO IT JIREN! 🔥🔥🔥","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":5,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-03T09:44:08.850Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper Body A","Lower Body A","Upper Body B","Lower Body B"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":9},{"r":10,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Pec Deck (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9},{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":10}],"note":"You need to take light enough so you can make all sets 12-15 and do 2 sec pause holding hands together in the end of the movement.\n\nFocus on squeezing inner elbows together!"},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":9,"x":2},{"r":10,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Lat Pull Down (Wide Grip)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":2},{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":10}],"note":"Focus on squeesing with your LATS!\n\nDrive your elbows down."},